[2026-09-20 12:19:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 102] STEP PURPOSE
[2026-09-20 12:19:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 102] --------------------------------------------------------------------------------
[2026-09-20 12:19:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 102]   Step 102 -- out-of-sample validation of the bipolar slip map.
[2026-09-20 12:19:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 102]   Every slip-map result so far (steps 086, 089) is an in-sample
[2026-09-20 12:19:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 102]   statement: the same 229 comets both define and evaluate the
[2026-09-20 12:19:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 102]   cos(2*theta) lapse profile.  A referee can therefore ask whether
[2026-09-20 12:19:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 102]   the map is real spatial structure or a fitted noise pattern.  This
[2026-09-20 12:19:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 102]   step converts the claim into a predictive one by testing the map
[2026-09-20 12:19:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 102]   on data it was not fitted to:
[2026-09-20 12:19:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 102]   T1  five-fold cross-validation on the pooled sample.  The map
[2026-09-20 12:19:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 102]   dtau(theta) = a + b*cos(2*theta) -- the pre-declared
[2026-09-20 12:19:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 102]   axisymmetric bipolar form measured in step 089, positive in
[2026-09-20 12:19:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 102]   both 60-deg lobes, negative in the 60-120 deg mid-band -- is
[2026-09-20 12:19:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 102]   fitted on each training fold and used to predict the signed
[2026-09-20 12:19:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 102]   planetary-subtracted slip dtau_unexplained of the held-out
[2026-09-20 12:19:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 102]   fold.  Skill is the out-of-sample Spearman correlation; the
[2026-09-20 12:19:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 102]   null is a theta-shuffle of the training labels (20000
[2026-09-20 12:19:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 102]   permutations, fixed seed).
[2026-09-20 12:19:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 102]   T2  cross-catalogue transfer.  The map fitted on the CODE cohort
[2026-09-20 12:19:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 102]   alone predicts the signed slips of the Warsaw cohort, and
[2026-09-20 12:19:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 102]   vice versa.  The two catalogues are independent orbit fits
[2026-09-20 12:19:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 102]   (different fitters, arcs and weightings), so a map that is a
[2026-09-20 12:19:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 102]   fitter artefact cannot transfer; a map that is sky structure
[2026-09-20 12:19:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 102]   must.
[2026-09-20 12:19:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 102]   T3  held-out sign accuracy.  The fitted map predicts the SIGN of
[2026-09-20 12:19:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 102]   each held-out slip; accuracy is scored against the binomial
[2026-09-20 12:19:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 102]   0.5 floor.  The sign pattern is the morphology the field
[2026-09-20 12:19:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 102]   actually predicts (positive in the lobes, negative in the
[2026-09-20 12:19:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 102]   mid-band), so this is the sharpest out-of-sample check.
[2026-09-20 12:19:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 102]   T4  amplitude calibration.  With the map fitted on one
[2026-09-20 12:19:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 102]   catalogue, predicted and observed median slips are compared
[2026-09-20 12:19:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 102]   bin-by-bin on the other -- a check that the transferred
[2026-09-20 12:19:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 102]   structure carries the right amplitude, not only the right
[2026-09-20 12:19:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 102]   ranking.
[2026-09-20 12:19:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 102]   The target channel throughout is dtau_unexplained (the catalogue
[2026-09-20 12:19:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 102]   slip with the REBOUND planetary baseline subtracted, step 065);
[2026-09-20 12:19:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 102]   the raw catalogue slip dtau_cat is reported as a secondary
[2026-09-20 12:19:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 102]   channel.  Nothing in this step re-tunes the axis, the cap width,
[2026-09-20 12:19:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 102]   or the harmonic order: the model has exactly two fitted
[2026-09-20 12:19:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 102]   coefficients (a, b) and one input angle.
[2026-09-20 12:19:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 102]   Inputs
[2026-09-20 12:19:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 102]   results/step_b30_proper_time_slip.csv   (229 comets: theta,
[2026-09-20 12:19:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 102]   dtau_cat, dtau_unexplained,
[2026-09-20 12:19:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 102]   cohort)
[2026-09-20 12:19:37 UTC] [INFO    ] [STEP 102]   Outputs
